---
layout: base.njk
title: Provenance
wide: true
description: "Proof-of-origin state: exact files, SHA-256 digests, timestamp status and how to verify independently."
---
<p class="kicker">Proof of origin · current state</p>
<h1>Provenance</h1>
<p class="lede">We're preserving the history of creation, not claiming ownership of ideas.</p>

<div class="table-scroll"><table>
  <caption class="kicker" style="text-align:left;padding-bottom:.5rem">Status as of {{ provenance.hashed_at_utc }}</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Evidence</th><th scope="col">State</th><th scope="col">Detail</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Founding package digests</td><td><span class="badge">published</span></td><td>{{ provenance.files.length }} files, SHA-256, from preservation commit <code>{{ provenance.preservation_commit | truncate(7, true, "") }}</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Founding transcript (<code>{{ provenance.founding_transcript.path }}</code>)</td><td><span class="badge {{ provenance.founding_transcript.state }}">{{ provenance.founding_transcript.state }}</span></td><td>{{ provenance.founding_transcript.note }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>OpenTimestamps proof</td><td><span class="badge {{ provenance.timestamp_state }}">{{ provenance.timestamp_state }}</span></td><td>{% if provenance.opentimestamps_proof_path %}<a href="{{ repoUrl }}/blob/main/{{ provenance.opentimestamps_proof_path }}"><code>{{ provenance.opentimestamps_proof_path }}</code></a> stamps <a href="{{ repoUrl }}/blob/main/{{ provenance.timestamped_artifact.path }}"><code>{{ provenance.timestamped_artifact.path }}</code></a> (SHA-256 <span class="hash">{{ provenance.timestamped_artifact.sha256 }}</span>), submitted {{ provenance.timestamped_artifact.stamped_utc }}.{% if provenance.timestamp_state == "pending" %} Pending: calendars have accepted it, but there is no Bitcoin attestation yet.{% endif %}{% if provenance.timestamp_state == "verified" %} Verified; see the next row.{% endif %}{% else %}No proof file exists.{% endif %}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Bitcoin attestation</td><td><span class="badge {% if not provenance.bitcoin_attestation_time_utc %}not-requested{% endif %}">{{ provenance.bitcoin_attestation_time_utc or "none" }}</span></td><td>{% if provenance.bitcoin_attestation %}Block {{ provenance.bitcoin_attestation.earliest_block_height }} (<span class="hash">{{ provenance.bitcoin_attestation.earliest_block_hash }}</span>), with later confirmations in blocks {{ provenance.bitcoin_attestation.additional_blocks | join(", ") }}. {{ provenance.verification_method }}{% else %}Reported only after verification succeeds.{% endif %}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>ChatGPT shared snapshot</td><td><span class="badge not-provided">not-provided</span></td><td>Even when one exists, a share link can change or be removed. It isn't an OpenAI certification.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>

<h2>What these digests do and don't show</h2>
<ul>
  {%- for l in provenance.limitations %}
  <li>{{ l }}</li>
  {%- endfor %}
  <li>None of this is a certificate of originality or of who came first, and no AI vendor has endorsed it.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Received package</h2>
{% if provenance.received_package %}
<p><code>{{ provenance.received_package.file }}</code> · {{ provenance.received_package.bytes }} bytes · SHA-256 <span class="hash">{{ provenance.received_package.sha256 }}</span></p>
<p>{{ provenance.received_package.note }}</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>Files</h2>
<p>Machine-readable: <a href="/provenance/launch-manifest.json"><code>launch-manifest.json</code></a>. These digests cover the files <em>as received</em>. Some, like the launch status files, have changed since, and you can see each change in the Git history.</p>
<div class="table-scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Path</th><th scope="col">Bytes</th><th scope="col">SHA-256</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for f in provenance.files %}
    <tr><td><code>{{ f.path }}</code></td><td class="num">{{ f.bytes }}</td><td class="hash">{{ f.sha256 }}</td></tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>

<h2>Verify it yourself</h2>
<pre><code>git clone {{ repoUrl }}.git && cd charter
git show {{ provenance.preservation_commit | truncate(7, true, "") }}:MANIFESTO.md | shasum -a 256
# compare with the table above, or regenerate the whole manifest:
node scripts/hash-manifest.mjs {{ provenance.preservation_commit | truncate(7, true, "") }} && git diff --stat provenance/</code></pre>
{% if provenance.opentimestamps_proof_path %}<pre><code>ots verify {{ provenance.opentimestamps_proof_path }}   # checks {{ provenance.timestamped_artifact.path }} against Bitcoin
shasum -a 256 -c {{ provenance.timestamped_artifact.path }}   # from the original package folder</code></pre>{% endif %}
<p>For more on timestamp proofs, follow <a href="{% sourceLink "provenance/VERIFY.md" %}"><code>provenance/VERIFY.md</code></a>. The full specification is in <a href="{% sourceLink "provenance/README.md" %}"><code>provenance/README.md</code></a>.</p>
